# The texts of the menu bar application, in the language of the United Kingdom.
#
# One entry per line: `key = value`. A line that starts with `#` is a
# comment and an empty line is ignored; a line that is neither is an error.
# The value may hold named placeholders in braces, for example `{streams}`.
# The placeholders are part of the contract: the code fills them in, and a
# placeholder without a value stays visible.
#
# The sentences of this language are the sentences of `en-US`. The British
# spelling is used where a word has one, and none of the texts of today
# holds such a word — the media folders and the library are spelled the same
# way in both languages. The two files are therefore nearly the same; that is
# expected, and it keeps the work of a translator small.

