# The messages of a failure. Every text names what happened, why it happened
# and what the user can do next (`UX-004`).
error.surface_unreachable = PhairDLNA couldn't connect to the server. Check that the server is running, then try again.
error.surface_unreadable = PhairDLNA couldn't read the server status. Try again in a moment.
error.answer_invalid = The server returned a response the app couldn't read. Try again; if this continues, check the server setup.
error.answer_unexpected = PhairDLNA received an unexpected response from the server. Try again. If it keeps happening, check the server setup.
error.token_refused = PhairDLNA couldn't verify its connection to the server. Check the server setup, then try again.
error.request_refused = The server couldn't complete this request. Check that it is running, then try again.
error.token_unreadable = PhairDLNA couldn't read its saved connection details. Restart the server or check its setup.
error.server_not_started = The server isn't running. Ask whoever set up PhairDLNA how to start it, then try again.
error.busy = The server is busy; the library was not read again. Try again in a moment.
error.scan_silent = The library was not read again: the server did not answer. Try again in a moment.
error.cannot_open = PhairDLNA couldn't open that item. Check that it is still available, then try again.
error.configuration_unreadable = PhairDLNA couldn't read its settings. The file may be missing or invalid. This app can't create its first settings file yet. If the settings file is missing and the command-line tool is available, run “phairdlna-cli setup” in Terminal. If the file already exists, ask whoever set up PhairDLNA to make it readable and valid. Then reopen the app.
error.worker_not_started = PhairDLNA couldn't start its background connection. Restart the app and try again.
error.preference_failed = PhairDLNA couldn't save this app setting. The change will be used until the app closes. Check the app's access to its settings, then try again.
error.diagnostics_save_failed = PhairDLNA couldn't save the diagnostics report to that location. Check that you can write there, choose another location, and try again.

